# November 22, 2026: a second scatter across Georgia, the state with the fewest places on the map (35), claimed with
# tools/choose.py --thinnest. Aimed at ground the two earlier batches left empty: the northwest (Rome, Adairsville,
# Rossville), the Atlanta edge (Roswell), the northeast mountains (Toccoa), middle Georgia (Macon, Juliette, High Falls,
# Indian Springs), the southwest (Columbus, Fort Gaines, Americus, Plains, Albany, Thomasville), the Okefenokee and Savannah.
# Facts from the linked sources only, read in this session: Wikipedia through tools/wiki_raw.py; Georgia State Parks,
# National Park Service, US Fish and Wildlife Service, Rome tourism office, Barnsley Resort, Cannonball House, Springer
# Opera House, Pebble Hill and Village at Indian Springs pages through tools/page.py. exploregeorgia.org was not used.
from data_b import N
from data_ma import W

